ankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T14:40:09-08:00","id":1362524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1362484#post1362484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you! That means a lot!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, thank you.<br /> <br /> I've essentially been on a bloodline deep dive today thanks to your products. I've been reminded that some Requiem bloodline ideas were bloody awful, and some were bloody brilliant. You've consistently seemed to capture the essence of them and focus ideas into usable 2E mechanics. I wish I'd noted down examples to remember, but there were a couple of times today I chuckled because of a manner in which something had been rendered, and I mean that as a positive.<br /> <br /> I suppose if I was going to ask a question I'd start with noting that your 2E Bloodline rules aesthetic is clearly based on the Khaibit preview from Rose Bailey's time as developer. Are you certain that's still the 2E bloodline mechanical focus? There's not been many published 2E bloodlines but the two I can think of, the Morbus and Bron, hew far closer to the 1E manner of doing things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12472-foozle","name":"Foozle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T15:04:36-08:00","id":1362527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foozle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1362524#post1362524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, thank you.<br /> <br /> I've essentially been on a bloodline deep dive today thanks to your products. I've been reminded that some Requiem bloodline ideas were bloody awful, and some were bloody brilliant. You've consistently seemed to capture the essence of them and focus ideas into usable 2E mechanics. I wish I'd noted down examples to remember, but there were a couple of times today I chuckled because of a manner in which something had been rendered, and I mean that as a positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happy to inspire a deep dive! There's lots of great stuff in the old books, even if some of it feels clunky now.<br /> <br /> And I had a great team for this! They really knocked all their bloodlines out of the park.<br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of the early Requiem bloodlines, especially the ones that are pretty wacky. One of my goals here was to cast away some of the oddness of the early bloodlines and make them more scary, while still fitting with the original concept. The Vedma, for example, are one I'm especially proud of, because the original Vedma are a very, VERY strange design all around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foozle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1362524#post1362524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose if I was going to ask a question I'd start with noting that your 2E Bloodline rules aesthetic is clearly based on the Khaibit preview from Rose Bailey's time as developer. Are you certain that's still the 2E bloodline mechanical focus? There's not been many published 2E bloodlines but the two I can think of, the Morbus and Bron, hew far closer to the 1E manner of doing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without spoiling anything, I do have some insight into 2E bloodlines, as I wrote on <b>Spilled Blood</b>, which is going to be the big book of (official) bloodlines that's coming out. I can't be more specific than that, because [REDACTED]. That's not to say <b>Devoted </b>is a preview (it's emphatically not), but I made sure material in B:tD could comfortably fit in Spilled Blood. That Khaibit Devotion chain style just might rear its head again. You never know...<br /> <br /> You'll see for yourself very soon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-21-2020, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T15:22:22-08:00","id":1362534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1362527#post1362527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm happy to inspire a deep dive! There's lots of great stuff in the old books, even if some of it feels clunky now.<br /> <br /> And I had a great team for this! They really knocked all their bloodlines out of the park.<br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of the early Requiem bloodlines, especially the ones that are pretty wacky. One of my goals here was to cast away some of the oddness of the early bloodlines and make them more scary, while still fitting with the original concept. The Vedma, for example, are one I'm especially proud of, because the original Vedma are a very, VERY strange design all around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Without spoiling anything, I do have some insight into 2E bloodlines, as I wrote on <b>Spilled Blood</b>, which is going to be the big book of (official) bloodlines that's coming out. I can't be more specific than that, because [REDACTED]. That's not to say <b>Devoted </b>is a preview (it's emphatically not), but I made sure material in B:tD could comfortably fit in Spilled Blood. That Khaibit Devotion chain style just might rear its head again. You never know...<br /> <br /> You'll see for yourself very soon!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T00:45:35-08:00","id":1362593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foozle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1362524#post1362524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, thank you.<br /> <br /> I've essentially been on a bloodline deep dive today thanks to your products. I've been reminded that some Requiem bloodline ideas were bloody awful, and some were bloody brilliant. You've consistently seemed to capture the essence of them and focus ideas into usable 2E mechanics. I wish I'd noted down examples to remember, but there were a couple of times today I chuckled because of a manner in which something had been rendered, and I mean that as a positive.<br /> <br /> I suppose if I was going to ask a question I'd start with noting that your 2E Bloodline rules aesthetic is clearly based on the Khaibit preview from Rose Bailey's time as developer. Are you certain that's still the 2E bloodline mechanical focus? There's not been many published 2E bloodlines but the two I can think of, the Morbus and Bron, hew far closer to the 1E manner of doing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodlines to me are one of the most important aspects of the game as they help provide diversity of powers and backgrounds so the work here is tremendous.<br /> <br /> As for the Morbus, I remember people (including myself) were disappointed to see they were pretty much a copy/paste in Dark Eras. So I'm happier with the way bloodlines are described here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T02:05:25-08:00","id":1362597,"title":"","content":"(I quite liked the way Cachexy was translated, but that's neither here nor there.) I'm glad people are enjoying our work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T04:35:45-08:00","id":1362618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1362593#post1362593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Morbus, I remember people (including myself) were disappointed to see they were pretty much a copy/paste in Dark Eras. So I'm happier with the way bloodlines are described here.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the bloodline is still mechanically sound and happen to follow current design principles, then what's there to change?<br /> <br /> Most of the negative criticism I've seen about Morbus in DE was from people who looked to the <i>experimental and unfinished</i> bloodlines on the Onyx Path blog* and started to expect new bloodlines or updates of old bloodlines to follow the same structures.<br /> <br /> <br /> To be honest I would've preferred the whole bloodline system to be revised so that we don't have families/dynasties, Covenant subgroups, and blood curses be mutually exclusive for no reason other than the fact that they're all made to fit a singular slot on the character sheet. Maybe Spilled Blood fixes at least some of that? I doubt it, but we'll see when it's finished.<br /> My personal preference would be for bloodlines to fill the same role as Legacies and Lodges from MtA and WtF, with dynasties having a smaller system to the side (maybe something which interacts with certain Skills?) and blood curses being their own things with unique rules to fit them.<br /> <br /> *Information which maybe should be added to their references in Bloodlines: The Devoted so people don't mistake them for finalised products with proper releases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-22-2020, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T14:44:41-08:00","id":1362736,"title":"","content":"Sorry, didn't mean to say the Morbus were bad or anything - just that, yes, after the direction bloodlines seemed to be taking, it was a bit surprising to see a more traditional take. No offense to the authors past or present.<br /> <br /> Still making my way through this product as I went back and read the Resurrected first (which was quite good!), but this is really nice work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T15:07:58-08:00","id":1362738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1362736#post1362736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, didn't mean to say the Morbus were bad or anything - just that, yes, after the direction bloodlines seemed to be taking, it was a bit surprising to see a more traditional take. No offense to the authors past or present.<br /> <br /> Still making my way through this product as I went back and read the Resurrected first (which was quite good!), but this is really nice work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really pleased this has been so well received (and we're number 1 on STV right now!)<br /> <br /> And if you like our work, make sure to leave a review if you have a moment! It's a little thing that can really help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T19:24:52-08:00","id":1363232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1362738#post1362738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really pleased this has been so well received (and we're number 1 on STV right now!)<br /> <br /> And if you like our work, make sure to leave a review if you have a moment! It's a little thing that can really help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Purchased, read, rated, and reviewed!<br /> <br /> I know it's not an entirely fair comparison, but I can say without hesitation I like this more than any of the 1e Bloodline books (Hidden, Legendary, or even Chosen). The devs seem to share my mechanical design sensibilities to a tee, and I haven't seen a single thing I would want to houserule or rewrite before using it at my table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]}