 be willing to grant their newly embraced fledgling a 'Sporting Chance' at Freedom? by not noting down their location or blood bonding them? <br /> <br /> Let Fate Decide their Destiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T01:31:37-07:00","id":1386933,"title":"","content":"Architects of the Monolith strike me as a Mystery Cult.<br /> Spina stuck me as just give them Resistance since their lore mentioned courage and they are basically experts in combat, not sure what to do for weakness but for boon I would probably make them better in one on one engagements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T02:19:44-07:00","id":1386936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1386933#post1386933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Architects of the Monolith strike me as a Mystery Cult.<br /> Spina stuck me as just give them Resistance since their lore mentioned courage and they are basically experts in combat, not sure what to do for weakness but for boon I would probably make them better in one on one engagements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resilience makes a lot of sense for them. I'm a big fan of bloodlines with all three physical Disciplines. I ended up giving them Dominate in the book because I thought it fit a little better as a thematic replacement for the old Discipline version of Courtoisie. I also shifted their bane to a compulsion to correct impoliteness rather than a difficulty being rude.<br /> <br /> If you weren't going to use the version of Courtoisie from Secrets of the Covenants in some way, I'd give them access to a Devotion or a Merit that makes it difficult for opponents to engage them in combat without also engaging them socially. Spina force people to fight on their home playing field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:31:30-07:00","id":1387040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1386936#post1386936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Resilience makes a lot of sense for them. I'm a big fan of bloodlines with all three physical Disciplines. I ended up giving them Dominate in the book because I thought it fit a little better as a thematic replacement for the old Discipline version of Courtoisie. I also shifted their bane to a compulsion to correct impoliteness rather than a difficulty being rude.<br /> <br /> If you weren't going to use the version of Courtoisie from Secrets of the Covenants in some way, I'd give them access to a Devotion or a Merit that makes it difficult for opponents to engage them in combat without also engaging them socially. Spina force people to fight on their home playing field.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dominate? How crass, one should be able to achieve their goals with reasoning and etiquette.<br /> Jokes aside giving Dominate and Majesty together is something I\u2019ve taken to treating as a sign to double check a bloodline just because it\u2019s so often the first thing that comes to mind. It can be the right answer but I\u2019ve been trying to avoid the path of least resistance in my own bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:21:40-07:00","id":1387058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1387040#post1387040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dominate? How crass, one should be able to achieve their goals with reasoning and etiquette.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey now, the Spina might be polite, but they ain't <i>nice</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1387040#post1387040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jokes aside giving Dominate and Majesty together is something I\u2019ve taken to treating as a sign to double check a bloodline just because it\u2019s so often the first thing that comes to mind. It can be the right answer but I\u2019ve been trying to avoid the path of least resistance in my own bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree. I gave the Asnam Protean/Animalism for much the same reason. Dominate makes sense, especially for their old fifth dot power, but it was way too on the nose.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:18:47-07:00","id":1387080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1387058#post1387058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey now, the Spina might be polite, but they ain't <i>nice</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Totally agree. I gave the Asnam Protean/Animalism for much the same reason. Dominate makes sense, especially for their old fifth dot power, but it was way too on the nose.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can\u2019t comment on them, I never got round to buying the books for the Covenants beginning with C (those law merits in Blood and Smoke took some time to accept). I\u2019ve never been a fan of dropping Clan disciplines from a bloodline, my inner optimiser wants to max it out before joining and the rest of me doesn\u2019t think it\u2019s fair to allow some players to max out 5 disciplines at in clan prices when others only get 4.<br /> Now what was that earlier about an official Bloodlines book? <br /> Also when are you going to do another actual play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T01:00:20-07:00","id":1387202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1362296-bloodlines-the-devoted-now-available-on-storytellers-vault?p=1387080#post1387080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can\u2019t comment on them, I never got round to buying the books for the Covenants beginning with C (those law merits in Blood and Smoke took some time to accept). I\u2019ve never been a fan of dropping Clan disciplines from a bloodline, my inner optimiser wants to max it out before joining and the rest of me doesn\u2019t think it\u2019s fair to allow some players to max out 5 disciplines at in clan prices when others only get 4.<br /> Now what was that earlier about an official Bloodlines book?<br /> Also when are you going to do another actual play?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm always sixes and sevens about changing out the spreads, too, but I tend to be okay with it if it's only one Discipline switching out, though it does get tricky with all-clan bloodlines (which are a bit more common in 2E). I do find that in my games, people usually take their bloodlines at chargen, so I haven't seen as much of an XP disparity. But really, there are a million ways to translate the old bloodlines, and a good argument can be made for just limiting bloodlines to the basic Disciplines and adding an inherent gift here and there. More like Changeling Kiths. That's a solid way to do it.<br /> <br /> As for an <i>official </i>bloodlines book, I know not, but me and the Devoted gang have STV plans for translating <b>Ancient Bloodlines</b>. However, we're also working on something else that'll probably come out sooner, but it's of a more...shadowy nature.<br /> <br /> As for another Requiem AP, you may have to wait till <i>Bloodlines 2 </i>comes out... &gt;_&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[]